---
import Policy, { type Outline } from '../layouts/Policy.astro';
import Row from '../components/Row.astro';
import { COMPANY, SITE } from '../data/site';

// How Zaaheen protects your memories (founder, session 67; both research
// reports: "Security page, recommended"). Facts checked in session 67: the
// vault is encrypted at rest with its key in Windows Credential Manager;
// Delete everything is cryptographic erasure (vault-app erasure.rs); sign-in
// is OAuth with PKCE in the browser (vault-account); the keeper's named pipe
// rejects remote clients (vault-app keeper/transport.rs); the account Worker
// holds no memories (workers/account record.ts). White label: no library,
// cipher or vendor names beyond what a reader needs.
const OUTLINE: Outline[] = [
  { id: 'computer', title: 'On your computer', topics: [
    { id: 'encrypted', title: 'Your memories are encrypted' },
    { id: 'key', title: 'The key never leaves your computer' },
    { id: 'local-only', title: 'Only apps on your computer can connect' },
    { id: 'erase', title: 'Delete everything means everything' },
  ] },
  { id: 'online', title: 'Online', topics: [
    { id: 'sign-in', title: 'Signing in' },
    { id: 'server', title: 'Our server holds no memories' },
  ] },
  { id: 'report', title: 'Reporting a problem', topics: [
    { id: 'beta', title: 'What we are still working on' },
    { id: 'vulnerability', title: 'Found a security issue?' },
  ] },
];
const topic = (id: string) =>
  OUTLINE.flatMap((s) => s.topics).find((t) => t.id === id)?.title ?? id;
const mail = `mailto:${COMPANY.email}`;
const lede = `${SITE.name} is built so that your memories are safe even if something goes wrong at our end, because they are never there. Here is how it protects them.`;
---
<Policy path="/security/" heading="Security" lede={lede} outline={OUTLINE}>
  <ul slot="summary">
    <li>Your memories are encrypted on your computer, and the key never leaves it.</li>
    <li>Only apps on your own computer can connect to Zaaheen, never anything from the
        internet.</li>
    <li>Our server holds no memories, so a break-in there could not expose them.</li>
    <li><em>Delete everything</em> destroys the key, so nothing can be recovered from the
        files, even from a copy.</li>
  </ul>

  <section id="computer" class="docs-section">
    <h2 class="docs-title">On your computer</h2>

    <Row id="encrypted" title={topic('encrypted')} where="At rest">
      <p>Your memories are encrypted on disk, and so is everything Zaaheen builds from them: the
         index it uses to search them and the summaries it writes when tidying up. Someone who copied the folder would
         see only scrambled data.</p>
    </Row>

    <Row id="key" title={topic('key')} where="Windows">
      <p>The key that unlocks your memories is created on your computer and kept in Windows' own
         secure store for your user account. It is never uploaded, never sent to us, and never
         written into the memory folder itself.</p>
    </Row>

    <Row id="local-only" title={topic('local-only')} where="Local only">
      <p>Your AI apps talk to Zaaheen through a private channel inside your computer. Zaaheen
         refuses connections from other computers and opens nothing to the internet, and each
         app has to introduce itself before Zaaheen answers.</p>
    </Row>

    <Row id="erase" title={topic('erase')} where="Settings › Your memories">
      <p><em>Delete everything</em> destroys the key first, then the files. Without the key,
         anything left behind on the disk, in a backup or in a copy can never be unlocked
         again.</p>
    </Row>
  </section>

  <section id="online" class="docs-section">
    <h2 class="docs-title">Online</h2>

    <Row id="sign-in" title={topic('sign-in')} where="Your browser">
      <p>You sign in through your own web browser, so the app never sees your password. It
         receives a sign-in token, kept in Windows' secure store, which it uses only to check your
         subscription. Signing in has nothing to do with the key to your memories.</p>
    </Row>

    <Row id="server" title={topic('server')} where="Our account service">
      <p>Our account service knows who you are and whether you have paid, and nothing else. It
         never receives your memories, so there is nothing there to leak. Everything between the
         app, our websites and our service travels encrypted.</p>
    </Row>
  </section>

  <section id="report" class="docs-section">
    <h2 class="docs-title">Reporting a problem</h2>

    <Row id="beta" title={topic('beta')} where="Beta">
      <p>While Zaaheen is in beta, its Windows installer is not yet code-signed, which is why
         Windows says the publisher is unknown when you install it. Signing comes before the full
         launch.</p>
    </Row>

    <Row id="vulnerability" title={topic('vulnerability')} where="Email">
      <p>If you think you have found a security problem, please email <a href={mail}>{COMPANY.email}</a>
         with "Security" in the subject, and tell us how to see it. Please give us a chance to fix
         it before telling anyone else. We will reply, keep you updated, and thank you publicly if
         you would like.</p>
    </Row>
  </section>
</Policy>
